/-!
# Derivation ideals and Zariski closedness of ideal order loci

For an algebra `R` over a commutative semiring `k` and an ideal `I` of `R`, the derivation ideal
`I.derivationIdeal k` is the ideal generated by `I` together with `D f` for every `f ∈ I` and
every `k`-derivation `D : Derivation k R R`. This generalizes the polynomial derivative ideal to
arbitrary algebras without choosing global coordinates.

By the Leibniz rule, every `k`-derivation lowers order at a prime by at most one, in every
characteristic and with no regularity or finiteness hypothesis:
`I.orderAt p ≤ (I.derivationIdeal k).orderAt p + 1`.

In characteristic zero, when `Ω[R⁄k]` is finitely generated and projective over `R` and the
localization `R_p` is regular local, the inequality is an equality:
`(I.derivationIdeal k).orderAt p = I.orderAt p - 1`. The proof uses formal smoothness of the
residue field `κ(p)` over `k` to inject the cotangent space `𝔪_p ⧸ 𝔪_p²` into
`κ(p) ⊗[R_p] Ω[R_p⁄k]`, lifts dual `κ(p)`-linear functionals to global `k`-derivations of `R`
up to a denominator outside `p`, and applies quasi-regularity of a regular system of parameters
together with Euler's homogeneous identity in `κ(p)[X₁, …, Xᵣ]`.

Iterating `n` times gives
`((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℕ∞) ≤ I.orderAt p ↔ (derivationIdeal k)^[n] I ≤ p.asIdeal`.
Consequently, on a regular ring with finitely generated projective Kähler differentials over a
characteristic-zero field — in particular on any smooth algebra or any regular finite-type algebra
over a characteristic-zero field — every order-threshold locus `{p | c ≤ I.orderAt p}` is Zariski
closed.

## Main definitions

* `Ideal.derivationIdeal`: the ideal generated by `I` and all values `D f` of `k`-derivations
  `D : Derivation k R R` on elements `f ∈ I`.

## Main results

* `Ideal.derivationIdeal_le_iff`: universal property of the derivation ideal.
* `Ideal.derivationIdeal_span`: generators of the derivation ideal from a generating set.
* `Ideal.orderAt_le_orderAt_derivationIdeal_add_one`: derivations lower order at any prime by at
  most one.
* `Ideal.orderAt_derivationIdeal`: in characteristic zero, at a regular prime of an algebra with
  finitely generated projective differentials, the derivation ideal lowers order by exactly one.
* `Ideal.natCast_add_one_le_orderAt_iff_iterate_derivationIdeal_le`: threshold characterization
  via iterated derivation ideals.
* `Ideal.isClosed_setOf_le_orderAt`: every order-threshold locus `{p | c ≤ I.orderAt p}` is
  Zariski closed.
* `Ideal.isClosed_setOf_le_orderAt_of_smooth`, `Ideal.isClosed_setOf_le_orderAt_of_finiteType`:
  closedness for smooth algebras and regular finite-type algebras over characteristic-zero fields.

## References

* E. Bierstone and P. D. Milman, *Canonical desingularization in characteristic zero by blowing
  up the maximum strata of a local invariant*, Invent. Math. 128 (1997), §4.1–4.2 and
  Proposition 4.12.
-/

